  "id": "minimal-pair",
  "term": "minimal pair",
  "definition": "A minimal pair is a pair of words or word-like forms that are the same except for one speech sound, such as an initial consonant or a vowel. In this context, researchers use minimal pairs to study how learners notice small phonetic differences when linking words to meanings.",
